# Added 2026-10-23 (2ad0b56c6b): ze used to refuse this ExaBGP command. It is the
# RFC 8956 Section 6.1 IPv6 route-target redirect, and ze must now send a valid
# UPDATE that a remote router acts on as it does on ExaBGP's: type 0x000D in
# attribute 25 naming route-target [2001:db8::5]:100, next hop untouched. ExaBGP
# f9bfb853b builds the same community (TrafficRedirectIPv6).
1:cmd:announce flow route destination 10.0.0.5/32 redirect [2001:db8::5]:100
1:raw:FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF:004B:02:00000034800E0C00018500000601200A0000054001010040020040050400000064C01914000D20010DB80000000000000000000000050064
